<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · river</p><h1 class="enc-title">Chebar</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Chebar canal</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Chebar was a canal near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nippur">Nippur</a> in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/babylonia">Babylonia</a>, called the 'great canal' in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cuneiform">cuneiform</a> records of the Persian period. In the Book of Ezekiel the prophet lives among the Judean exiles settled by the Chebar and sees his visions there. The communities of deportees along such canals kept their own leaders and identity during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/babylonian-captivity">Babylonian captivity</a>.</p></div>
